    <!-- About Circle (SETTINGS_AND_POLISH 4, styled per V2 5) -->
    <string name="about_kicker">WHAT IT IS</string>
    <string name="about_headline">A small place for the people you actually know.</string>
    <string name="about_how_caps">HOW IT\'S DIFFERENT</string>
    <string name="about_p1_lead">Just your friends.</string>
    <string name="about_p1">You ask, they accept. No followers, and no strangers in your feed.</string>
    <string name="about_p2_lead">See what they\'re up to.</string>
    <string name="about_p2">Newest first, in the order it happened. Nothing is ranked or pushed at you.</string>
    <string name="about_p3_lead">It ends.</string>
    <string name="about_p3">Circle tells you when you\'re caught up, so you can close it and go and see them.</string>
    <string name="about_p4_lead">Quiet likes.</string>
    <string name="about_p4">Only the person you liked sees it. Nobody is performing for a score.</string>
    <string name="about_p5_lead">Made for real life.</string>
    <string name="about_p5">Events and groups take you out of the house and back to real people.</string>
    <string name="about_p6_lead">No ads.</string>
    <string name="about_p6">Circle runs on a small membership, and your data is never sold.</string>
    <string name="about_why_caps">WHY \"CIRCLE\"?</string>
    <string name="about_why_body">It\'s your circle of friends. And a circle closes: when you\'ve seen everyone\'s day, the circle is closed, and you\'re done. (That\'s why the name ends with a full stop.)</string>

    <!-- Why I built it -->
    <string name="why_p1">I built Circle because the apps I used to love for keeping up with friends turned into endless scrolling. I wanted a place where I open the app, see what my friends are up to, and close it again. No tricks to keep me there.</string>
    <string name="why_p2">If you want a bigger circle, make an event, go outside and meet someone. Then come back and tell your friends about it.</string>
    <string name="why_p3">Thank you for being here.</string>
    <string name="why_signature" translatable="false">Shashank</string>
</resources>
